# Privileged IP work product — fail-closed allowlist.
#
# Everything in this directory is ignored unless named below. That direction is
# deliberate: a denylist protects the files somebody remembered to list, and the
# risk here is the claim chart nobody thought to add. A new privileged file
# dropped into this directory is ignored by default and has to be argued into
# version control, which is the correct order for this material.
#
# WHAT MAY BE TRACKED (founder instruction, 2026-08-11): register ID, status and
# design-around gate. Not claim-level analysis of a RED family — no claim
# numbers, no "reads onto", no infringement or anticipation reading. That
# material is extracted to a counsel packet by
# research/scripts/export_privileged_packet.py and kept outside the repository.
#
# Path exclusion is only half the control. Claim-level text can also appear
# inside an allowlisted file — it already did once, in the register's own
# `note:` field — so scripts/ip_privilege_guard.py scans content as well, and
# the pre-commit hook runs it. Neither control replaces the other.
#
# This file cannot un-ignore anything inside a subdirectory: git will not
# descend into an excluded directory to find a negation. There are no
# subdirectories here today. Adding one means adding its own rule.

*
!.gitignore
!TECHNOLOGY_INTAKE_REGISTER.yaml
!V4_DISCLOSURE_REGISTRY.yaml
